//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  FVG + IFVG SWING STRATEGY  —  ICT / Smart Money Concepts  —  5m execution / 15m bias
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
//  HOW TO USE THIS STRATEGY IN THE STRATEGY TESTER
//  ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  1. Recommended symbols : MES1! / MNQ1! (micro futures, continuous contract). ES1!/NQ1! work
//     too, but micros let you size realistically on a small account.
//  2. Recommended chart   : 5-minute. The HTF bias is pulled from 15m internally — do NOT change
//     the chart timeframe above 15m or the bias becomes meaningless.
//  3. Position sizing     : Default is "Risk % of Equity" at 1% on a $25,000 initial capital.
//     Example ($25k account, MES, point value $5, tick $1.25):
//        risk 1% = $250. A 10-point (40-tick) stop risks $50/contract → 5 contracts.
//     The script computes this for you from the actual stop distance. Switch to
//     "Fixed Contracts" if you prefer a constant size.
//  4. Commission/slippage : Defaults assume ~$0.75/contract/side commission+fees and 1 tick of
//     slippage per fill. Adjust in the strategy() header for your broker.
//  5. WARNINGS — read before trusting any backtest:
//     • TradingView fills orders on OHLC of the chart bars only. Intrabar stop/target sequencing
//       on a 5m bar is APPROXIMATED — always validate entries with Bar Replay before going live.
//     • Continuous futures contracts (MES1!) contain roll gaps that can distort results.
//     • Signals are evaluated on CLOSED bars and orders fill on the NEXT bar open
//       (calc_on_every_tick = false, process_orders_on_close = false). This is deliberately
//       conservative and non-repainting, but live fills will differ slightly.
//     • This is a STARTING POINT for research, not financial advice and not a finished system.
//       Forward-test on paper before risking real money.
//  6. NO RESULTS IN THE STRATEGY TESTER? Work through this list:
//     a) Open the "Strategy Tester" tab at the BOTTOM of the chart (it does not pop up on its own).
//     b) If it says "no data" / no trades were generated: make sure you are on a 5-MINUTE chart of
//        MES1!/MNQ1! and scroll left so enough history is loaded (the 15m EMA needs ~50 bars of
//        15m data plus pivot warm-up before the first signal can even exist).
//     c) Margin: this script sets margin_long/margin_short = 5 (futures-style leverage). If you
//        change initial_capital or trade full-size contracts, entries that exceed available margin
//        are SILENTLY skipped — set both margins to 0 to rule this out.
//     d) Loosen filters step by step to find the blocker: Confluences required → 0,
//        Bias method → "Off (no bias filter)", Restrict to NY RTH → off, Minimum FVG size → Off.
//        If trades appear, re-tighten one input at a time.
//     e) A red/orange (!) next to the strategy name on the chart = runtime error — click it and
//        fix (or report) the message. The tester stays empty while an error is active.
//
//  STRATEGY LOGIC SUMMARY
//  ──────────────────────
//  • Detects 3-candle Fair Value Gaps (FVG) on the chart timeframe (5m intended).
//  • When price closes THROUGH an FVG, the zone flips into an Inversion FVG (IFVG) and acts as
//    support/resistance in the opposite direction.
//  • Entries: price taps a bullish FVG/IFVG (long) or bearish FVG/IFVG (short) and closes with a
//    rejection, WITH 15-minute EMA bias agreement, WITH >= N of the optional confluences:
//    displacement, liquidity sweep, market-structure shift, NY kill-zone timing.
//  • Exits: structural stop beyond the zone/swing (+ ATR buffer), scale-out at TP1, runner to a
//    fixed R multiple or an ATR trailing stop. Optional break-even after TP1.
//  • Filters: NY RTH session, optional kill zones, max trades per direction per day, optional
//    end-of-day flat, and a commented-out daily loss limit you can enable.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// NOTE: default_qty_* in the declaration is only a fallback. Actual size is computed per-trade
// from the "Position Sizing" inputs (Fixed Contracts OR Risk % of Equity) in section 7.
//
// CRITICAL for futures: TradingView defaults margin_long/margin_short to 100% (cash account).
// One MES contract is ~$30k notional > $25k initial capital, so with the default EVERY entry is
// silently rejected and the Strategy Tester stays empty. margin = 5 approximates real intraday
// futures margin (MES day margin ≈ $1.5-2k vs ~$30k notional). Set both to 0 to disable margin
// checks entirely.
strategy(
     title                    = "FVG + IFVG Swing Strategy [5m MES/MNQ]",
     shorttitle               = "FVG/IFVG Swing",
     overlay                  = true,
     initial_capital          = 25000,
     currency                 = currency.USD,
     default_qty_type         = strategy.fixed,
     default_qty_value        = 1,
     commission_type          = strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, // futures: $ per contract per fill
     commission_value         = 0.75,                                  // ~all-in cost per side for micros
     slippage                 = 1,                                     // 1 tick of slippage per fill
     margin_long              = 5,                                     // see CRITICAL note above
     margin_short             = 5,
     calc_on_every_tick       = false,                                 // evaluate on closed bars only
     process_orders_on_close  = false,                                 // fills happen on next bar open
     pyramiding               = 0,
     max_bars_back            = 500,
     max_boxes_count          = 500,
     max_labels_count         = 500,
     max_lines_count          = 500)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  1. INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── Position sizing & risk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_RISK = "Position Sizing & Risk"
sizingMode     = input.string("Risk % of Equity", "Sizing mode", options = ["Risk % of Equity", "Fixed Contracts"], group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "Risk % of Equity: contracts = floor(equity * risk% / $risk-per-contract at the stop). Fixed Contracts: always trade the same size. Futures users: 1 MES point = $5, 1 MNQ point = $2.")
riskPct        = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10, step = 0.25, group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "Only used in 'Risk % of Equity' mode. 1% of $25k = $250 risked per trade.")
fixedContracts = input.int(1, "Fixed contracts", minval = 1, group = G_RISK,
     tooltip = "Only used in 'Fixed Contracts' mode.")

// ── FVG / IFVG detection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_FVG = "FVG / IFVG Detection"
useFvgEntries   = input.bool(true,  "Trade fresh FVGs",  group = G_FVG)
useIfvgEntries  = input.bool(true,  "Trade IFVGs (inverted FVGs)", group = G_FVG)
enableIFVG      = input.bool(true,  "Enable inversion logic", group = G_FVG,
     tooltip = "ON: an FVG that price closes through flips into an opposite-polarity IFVG zone. OFF: a violated FVG is simply removed.")
minSizeMode     = input.string("% of ATR", "Minimum FVG size filter", options = ["Off", "Ticks", "% of ATR"], group = G_FVG)
minSizeTicks    = input.int(4, "Min size (ticks)", minval = 1, group = G_FVG)
minSizeAtrPct   = input.float(25.0, "Min size (% of ATR)", minval = 1, step = 5, group = G_FVG)
requireDispFvg  = input.bool(false, "Only track FVGs created by displacement", group = G_FVG,
     tooltip = "Hard filter at creation time. Leave OFF to track all gaps and let displacement act as a soft confluence instead.")
dispAtrMult     = input.float(1.0, "Displacement: middle-candle body >= ATR x", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = G_FVG)
maxZoneAge      = input.int(120, "Zone expiry (bars)", minval = 10, group = G_FVG,
     tooltip = "Zones older than this are dropped. 120 bars on 5m = one full RTH session.")
maxTrackedZones = input.int(40, "Max tracked zones", minval = 5, maxval = 100, group = G_FVG)

// ── Higher timeframe bias ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_HTF = "Higher Timeframe Bias (15m)"
htfTf      = input.timeframe("15", "Bias timeframe", group = G_HTF)
biasMode   = input.string("Price vs EMA", "Bias method", options = ["Price vs EMA", "EMA Slope", "Off (no bias filter)"], group = G_HTF,
     tooltip = "Price vs EMA: bullish when the last CONFIRMED 15m close is above the 15m EMA. EMA Slope: bullish when the 15m EMA is rising. Off: take both directions regardless of HTF — useful for debugging why no trades fire.")
htfEmaLen  = input.int(50, "HTF EMA length", minval = 5, group = G_HTF)
showHtfEma = input.bool(true, "Plot HTF EMA", group = G_HTF)
showBiasBg = input.bool(true, "Background-tint active bias", group = G_HTF)

// ── Entry logic & confluences ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_ENTRY = "Entry Logic & Confluences"
entryMode      = input.string("Market", "Entry type", options = ["Market", "Limit (zone midpoint)"], group = G_ENTRY,
     tooltip = "Market: enter next bar open after a valid tap+rejection close. Limit: rest a limit at the tapped zone's midpoint (consequent encroachment).")
limitExpiryBars= input.int(6, "Limit order expiry (bars)", minval = 1, group = G_ENTRY)
minConfluences = input.int(2, "Confluences required (of those enabled)", minval = 0, maxval = 4, group = G_ENTRY)
useDispConf    = input.bool(true, "Confluence: displacement created the zone", group = G_ENTRY)
useSweepConf   = input.bool(true, "Confluence: recent liquidity sweep", group = G_ENTRY)
useMssConf     = input.bool(true, "Confluence: recent market structure shift", group = G_ENTRY)
useKzConf      = input.bool(true, "Confluence: inside NY kill zone", group = G_ENTRY)
swingLen       = input.int(5, "Swing pivot length (bars each side)", minval = 2, group = G_ENTRY)
sweepLookback  = input.int(12, "Liquidity sweep valid for (bars)", minval = 1, group = G_ENTRY)
mssLookback    = input.int(20, "MSS valid for (bars)", minval = 1, group = G_ENTRY)

// ── Trade management ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_EXIT = "Trade Management"
stopMode       = input.string("Zone + ATR buffer", "Stop-loss placement", options = ["Zone + ATR buffer", "Swing + ATR buffer", "Fixed Ticks"], group = G_EXIT)
stopAtrMult    = input.float(0.5, "Stop ATR buffer multiplier", minval = 0.0, step = 0.1, group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "Extra room beyond the zone edge / swing point, in ATR multiples.")
stopFixedTicks = input.int(40, "Fixed stop (ticks)", minval = 4, group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "Only used in 'Fixed Ticks' mode. 40 ticks = 10 MES points = $50/contract.")
rrTarget       = input.float(2.0, "Final target (R multiple)", minval = 1.0, step = 0.25, group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "Minimum 2.0 recommended per the strategy design.")
useScaleOut    = input.bool(true, "Scale out at TP1", group = G_EXIT)
tp1RR          = input.float(1.5, "TP1 (R multiple)", minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = G_EXIT)
scaleOutPct    = input.float(50, "TP1 size (% of position)", minval = 10, maxval = 90, step = 10, group = G_EXIT)
runnerMode     = input.string("Fixed R Target", "Runner exit", options = ["Fixed R Target", "ATR Trail"], group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "Fixed R Target: runner exits at the final R multiple. ATR Trail: after price reaches TP1, trail the runner by ATR x multiplier.")
trailAtrMult   = input.float(1.5, "Trail distance (ATR x)", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = G_EXIT)
useBreakeven   = input.bool(true, "Move stop to break-even after TP1 fills", group = G_EXIT)
beOffsetTicks  = input.int(1, "Break-even offset (ticks)", minval = 0, group = G_EXIT,
     tooltip = "Ticks of profit locked in when the stop moves to break-even.")
atrLen         = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = G_EXIT)

// ── Session, time & daily limits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_TIME = "Session & Daily Limits"
tz            = input.string("America/New_York", "Timezone", group = G_TIME)
useSession    = input.bool(true, "Restrict to NY RTH session", group = G_TIME)
sessionStr    = input.session("0930-1600", "RTH session", group = G_TIME)
useKillZones  = input.bool(false, "HARD filter: only trade inside kill zones", group = G_TIME,
     tooltip = "OFF by default — kill-zone timing still counts as a soft confluence above.")
kzStr         = input.session("0930-1100,1400-1530", "Kill zones", group = G_TIME)
useEodClose   = input.bool(true, "Flatten at end of day", group = G_TIME)
eodStr        = input.session("1550-1600", "Flatten window", group = G_TIME)
maxLongsDay   = input.int(2, "Max long entries per day", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_TIME)
maxShortsDay  = input.int(2, "Max short entries per day", minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = G_TIME)

// ── Visuals ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_VIS = "Visuals"
showZones   = input.bool(true, "Draw FVG/IFVG boxes", group = G_VIS)
colBullFvg  = input.color(color.new(#26a69a, 80), "Bullish FVG", group = G_VIS)
colBearFvg  = input.color(color.new(#ef5350, 80), "Bearish FVG", group = G_VIS)
colBullIfvg = input.color(color.new(#2962ff, 72), "Bullish IFVG (flipped bear FVG)", group = G_VIS)
colBearIfvg = input.color(color.new(#ff6d00, 72), "Bearish IFVG (flipped bull FVG)", group = G_VIS)
colDead     = color.new(color.gray, 92)          // frozen/expired zones

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  2. CORE SERIES & SESSION STATE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

atr = ta.atr(atrLen)

// Session windows. time() returns na outside the window, so "not na" = inside.
inRTH  = not na(time(timeframe.period, sessionStr, tz))
inKZ   = not na(time(timeframe.period, kzStr, tz))
eodNow = useEodClose and not na(time(timeframe.period, eodStr, tz))

// Combined hard time filter for NEW entries.
timeOK = (not useSession or inRTH) and (not useKillZones or inKZ) and not eodNow

// New calendar day → reset daily counters.
newDay = timeframe.change("D")

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  3. HIGHER TIMEFRAME BIAS (non-repainting)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  We request the value of the PREVIOUS (confirmed) 15m bar with lookahead OFF. This means the
//  bias never repaints: it only updates once a 15m bar has fully closed.

htfEma      = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, ta.ema(close, htfEmaLen)[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
htfCloseCnf = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, htfTf, close[1],                    lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)

// "EMA Slope" compares the confirmed HTF EMA against its value a few chart bars back — a simple
// rising/falling proxy that avoids a second security() call.
biasOff  = biasMode == "Off (no bias filter)"
biasBull = biasOff ? true : biasMode == "Price vs EMA" ? htfCloseCnf > htfEma : htfEma > htfEma[3]
biasBear = biasOff ? true : biasMode == "Price vs EMA" ? htfCloseCnf < htfEma : htfEma < htfEma[3]
// Note: while htfEma is still na (warm-up), both flags are false → no trades. That is intended
// (unless bias is Off, in which case both directions are always allowed).

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  4. MARKET STRUCTURE: PIVOTS, LIQUIDITY SWEEPS, MSS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Pivots confirm swingLen bars after the extreme — inherently delayed but non-repainting.

ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swingLen, swingLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low, swingLen, swingLen)

var float lastPivotHigh = na   // most recent confirmed swing high (buy-side liquidity)
var float lastPivotLow  = na   // most recent confirmed swing low  (sell-side liquidity)
if not na(ph)
    lastPivotHigh := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPivotLow := pl

// Liquidity sweep: price wicks THROUGH the last swing point but closes back on the original side
// (stop-run / turtle-soup behaviour).
bullSweep = not na(lastPivotLow)  and low  < lastPivotLow  and close > lastPivotLow
bearSweep = not na(lastPivotHigh) and high > lastPivotHigh and close < lastPivotHigh

// Market Structure Shift (simplified): a CLOSE through the last confirmed swing point.
bullMss = not na(lastPivotHigh) and close > lastPivotHigh and close[1] <= lastPivotHigh
bearMss = not na(lastPivotLow)  and close < lastPivotLow  and close[1] >= lastPivotLow

// "Recent" flags — the event stays valid as a confluence for N bars.
bullSweepRecent = nz(ta.barssince(bullSweep), 99999) <= sweepLookback
bearSweepRecent = nz(ta.barssince(bearSweep), 99999) <= sweepLookback
bullMssRecent   = nz(ta.barssince(bullMss),   99999) <= mssLookback
bearMssRecent   = nz(ta.barssince(bearMss),   99999) <= mssLookback

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  5. FVG / IFVG DETECTION & ZONE MANAGEMENT
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// A tracked zone. Polarity (isBull) FLIPS when the zone inverts into an IFVG.
type Zone
    float top
    float bottom
    bool  isBull           // current polarity: true = acts as support (long zone)
    bool  isInverted       // true once the zone has flipped into an IFVG
    bool  hadDisplacement  // was the ORIGINAL gap created by a displacement candle?
    int   createdBar
    int   flipBar          // bar_index at inversion (na until inverted)
    box   bx

var zones = array.new<Zone>()

// Minimum gap-size filter (ticks or % of ATR).
gapSizeOK(float gapSize) =>
    switch minSizeMode
        "Ticks"    => gapSize >= minSizeTicks * syminfo.mintick
        "% of ATR" => gapSize >= atr * minSizeAtrPct / 100.0
        => true

// ── 5a. Detect new FVGs (confirmed on close of the 3rd candle → non-repainting) ────────────────
// Bullish FVG : current low  > high two bars ago (gap between candle 1's high and candle 3's low).
// Bearish FVG : current high < low  two bars ago.
// The MIDDLE candle (bar[1]) is the displacement candle.
bullDisp = (close[1] - open[1]) >= dispAtrMult * atr   // strong bullish middle-candle body
bearDisp = (open[1] - close[1]) >= dispAtrMult * atr   // strong bearish middle-candle body

newBullFvg = low > high[2]  and gapSizeOK(low - high[2])  and (not requireDispFvg or bullDisp)
newBearFvg = high < low[2] and gapSizeOK(low[2] - high) and (not requireDispFvg or bearDisp)

if newBullFvg
    b = box.new(bar_index - 2, low, bar_index, high[2],
         border_color = showZones ? color.new(colBullFvg, 40) : na,
         bgcolor      = showZones ? colBullFvg : na,
         text = "FVG", text_color = color.new(colBullFvg, 30), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)
    zones.push(Zone.new(low, high[2], true, false, bullDisp, bar_index, int(na), b))

if newBearFvg
    b = box.new(bar_index - 2, low[2], bar_index, high,
         border_color = showZones ? color.new(colBearFvg, 40) : na,
         bgcolor      = showZones ? colBearFvg : na,
         text = "FVG", text_color = color.new(colBearFvg, 30), text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)
    zones.push(Zone.new(low[2], high, false, false, bearDisp, bar_index, int(na), b))

// ── 5b. Update / invert / expire existing zones ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Iterate backwards so removal while looping is safe.
if zones.size() > 0
    for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
        z = zones.get(i)
        box.set_right(z.bx, bar_index)     // keep extending the active zone to the right
        bool kill = false

        if not z.isInverted
            // A fresh FVG is violated when price CLOSES through its far side.
            if z.isBull and close < z.bottom
                if enableIFVG
                    // Bullish FVG broken downward → becomes a BEARISH IFVG (resistance).
                    z.isBull     := false
                    z.isInverted := true
                    z.flipBar    := bar_index
                    box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, showZones ? colBearIfvg : na)
                    box.set_border_color(z.bx, showZones ? color.new(colBearIfvg, 30) : na)
                    box.set_border_style(z.bx, line.style_dashed)
                    box.set_text(z.bx, "IFVG")
                    box.set_text_color(z.bx, color.new(colBearIfvg, 20))
                else
                    kill := true
            else if not z.isBull and close > z.top
                if enableIFVG
                    // Bearish FVG broken upward → becomes a BULLISH IFVG (support).
                    z.isBull     := true
                    z.isInverted := true
                    z.flipBar    := bar_index
                    box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, showZones ? colBullIfvg : na)
                    box.set_border_color(z.bx, showZones ? color.new(colBullIfvg, 30) : na)
                    box.set_border_style(z.bx, line.style_dashed)
                    box.set_text(z.bx, "IFVG")
                    box.set_text_color(z.bx, color.new(colBullIfvg, 20))
                else
                    kill := true
        else
            // An IFVG dies when price closes back through its far side (second inversion = chop).
            if z.isBull and close < z.bottom
                kill := true
            else if not z.isBull and close > z.top
                kill := true

        // Age expiry keeps the chart and the zone array clean.
        if bar_index - z.createdBar > maxZoneAge
            kill := true

        if kill
            box.set_bgcolor(z.bx, showZones ? colDead : na)   // freeze & dim instead of deleting
            box.set_border_color(z.bx, na)
            box.set_right(z.bx, bar_index)
            zones.remove(i)

// Hard cap on tracked zones (oldest dropped first) to protect performance.
if zones.size() > maxTrackedZones
    old = zones.shift()
    box.set_bgcolor(old.bx, showZones ? colDead : na)
    box.set_border_color(old.bx, na)

// ── 5c. Tap detection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A LONG tap: this bar's low trades into a bullish zone, but the bar CLOSES back above the zone
// midpoint (rejection). Mirror for shorts. Newest zones are checked first. Zones cannot signal on
// the bar they were created or inverted on.
bool  bullTap     = false
float tapTopL     = na
float tapBotL     = na
bool  tapDispL    = false
bool  bearTap     = false
float tapTopS     = na
float tapBotS     = na
bool  tapDispS    = false

if zones.size() > 0
    for i = zones.size() - 1 to 0
        z = zones.get(i)
        // Which signal source is this zone allowed to be?
        sourceOK = z.isInverted ? useIfvgEntries : useFvgEntries
        matured  = bar_index > z.createdBar and (na(z.flipBar) or bar_index > z.flipBar)
        if sourceOK and matured
            mid = math.avg(z.top, z.bottom)
            if z.isBull and not bullTap and low <= z.top and close > mid
                bullTap  := true
                tapTopL  := z.top
                tapBotL  := z.bottom
                tapDispL := z.hadDisplacement
            if not z.isBull and not bearTap and high >= z.bottom and close < mid
                bearTap  := true
                tapTopS  := z.top
                tapBotS  := z.bottom
                tapDispS := z.hadDisplacement
        if bullTap and bearTap
            break

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  6. CONFLUENCE SCORING & SIGNALS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Count how many ENABLED confluences agree. minConfluences of them must be present (default 2).
int confLong = 0
confLong += (useDispConf  and tapDispL)        ? 1 : 0
confLong += (useSweepConf and bullSweepRecent) ? 1 : 0
confLong += (useMssConf   and bullMssRecent)   ? 1 : 0
confLong += (useKzConf    and inKZ)            ? 1 : 0

int confShort = 0
confShort += (useDispConf  and tapDispS)        ? 1 : 0
confShort += (useSweepConf and bearSweepRecent) ? 1 : 0
confShort += (useMssConf   and bearMssRecent)   ? 1 : 0
confShort += (useKzConf    and inKZ)            ? 1 : 0

// Daily entry counters (reset each new day, incremented on actual FILLS in section 7).
var int longsToday  = 0
var int shortsToday = 0
if newDay
    longsToday  := 0
    shortsToday := 0

// ── OPTIONAL: DAILY LOSS LIMIT (uncomment to enable) ────────────────────────────────────────────
// maxDailyLossUSD = input.float(500, "Max daily loss ($)", minval = 50, group = G_TIME)
// var float dayStartEquity = na
// if newDay
//     dayStartEquity := strategy.equity
// dailyLossHit = not na(dayStartEquity) and (strategy.equity - dayStartEquity) <= -maxDailyLossUSD
// if dailyLossHit and strategy.position_size != 0
//     strategy.close_all(comment = "Daily loss limit")
// ...then add `and not dailyLossHit` to longSignal/shortSignal below.

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

longSignal  = bullTap and biasBull and confLong  >= minConfluences and timeOK and flat and longsToday  < maxLongsDay
shortSignal = bearTap and biasBear and confShort >= minConfluences and timeOK and flat and shortsToday < maxShortsDay

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  7. POSITION SIZING, ENTRIES & EXITS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Contracts from dollar risk: floor(risk$ / (stop distance in points * point value)), min 1.
// syminfo.pointvalue = $5 for MES, $2 for MNQ, $50 for ES, $20 for NQ.
calcQty(float stopDistPoints) =>
    float q = fixedContracts
    if sizingMode == "Risk % of Equity"
        riskDollars     = strategy.equity * riskPct / 100.0
        perContractRisk = stopDistPoints * syminfo.pointvalue
        q := perContractRisk > 0 ? math.max(1, math.floor(riskDollars / perContractRisk)) : 1
    q

// Trade-state vars shared by the (single) open position. na when flat.
var float slAct      = na     // active stop level
var float tp1Act     = na     // active scale-out target
var float tp2Act     = na     // active final target
var float initialQty = na     // contracts at fill (to detect the TP1 partial)
var bool  beDone     = false  // break-even already applied?
var int   pendingBar = na     // bar a limit entry order was submitted (for expiry)

// ── 7a. Submit entry orders on a signal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if longSignal
    // Expected entry: next bar ~close for market orders, zone midpoint for limit orders.
    expEntry = entryMode == "Market" ? close : math.avg(tapTopL, tapBotL)
    // Structural stop below the zone or swing, plus an ATR buffer.
    slLvl = switch stopMode
        "Zone + ATR buffer"  => tapBotL - atr * stopAtrMult
        "Swing + ATR buffer" => nz(lastPivotLow, tapBotL) - atr * stopAtrMult
        => expEntry - stopFixedTicks * syminfo.mintick
    slLvl := math.min(slLvl, expEntry - syminfo.mintick)   // safety: stop must sit below entry
    risk  = expEntry - slLvl
    qty   = calcQty(risk)
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    strategy.cancel("Short")
    if entryMode == "Market"
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty)
        pendingBar := na
    else
        strategy.entry("Long", strategy.long, qty, limit = expEntry)
        pendingBar := bar_index
    // Provisional exit levels (refined with the actual fill price in 7b).
    slAct  := slLvl
    tp1Act := expEntry + tp1RR * risk
    tp2Act := expEntry + rrTarget * risk

if shortSignal
    expEntry = entryMode == "Market" ? close : math.avg(tapTopS, tapBotS)
    slLvl = switch stopMode
        "Zone + ATR buffer"  => tapTopS + atr * stopAtrMult
        "Swing + ATR buffer" => nz(lastPivotHigh, tapTopS) + atr * stopAtrMult
        => expEntry + stopFixedTicks * syminfo.mintick
    slLvl := math.max(slLvl, expEntry + syminfo.mintick)   // safety: stop must sit above entry
    risk  = slLvl - expEntry
    qty   = calcQty(risk)
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    strategy.cancel("Short")
    if entryMode == "Market"
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty)
        pendingBar := na
    else
        strategy.entry("Short", strategy.short, qty, limit = expEntry)
        pendingBar := bar_index
    slAct  := slLvl
    tp1Act := expEntry - tp1RR * risk
    tp2Act := expEntry - rrTarget * risk

// Expire unfilled limit entries.
if flat and not na(pendingBar) and bar_index - pendingBar >= limitExpiryBars
    strategy.cancel("Long")
    strategy.cancel("Short")
    pendingBar := na

// ── 7b. On fill: recompute exact levels from the real average price ─────────────────────────────
justOpenedLong  = strategy.position_size > 0 and strategy.position_size[1] <= 0
justOpenedShort = strategy.position_size < 0 and strategy.position_size[1] >= 0

if justOpenedLong
    avg = strategy.position_avg_price
    if stopMode == "Fixed Ticks"
        slAct := avg - stopFixedTicks * syminfo.mintick
    slAct      := math.min(slAct, avg - syminfo.mintick)
    riskPts     = avg - slAct
    tp1Act     := avg + tp1RR * riskPts
    tp2Act     := avg + rrTarget * riskPts
    initialQty := math.abs(strategy.position_size)
    beDone     := false
    pendingBar := na
    longsToday += 1

if justOpenedShort
    avg = strategy.position_avg_price
    if stopMode == "Fixed Ticks"
        slAct := avg + stopFixedTicks * syminfo.mintick
    slAct      := math.max(slAct, avg + syminfo.mintick)
    riskPts     = slAct - avg
    tp1Act     := avg - tp1RR * riskPts
    tp2Act     := avg - rrTarget * riskPts
    initialQty := math.abs(strategy.position_size)
    beDone     := false
    pendingBar := na
    shortsToday += 1

// ── 7c. Manage exits every bar (orders are modified in place by re-issuing the same IDs) ────────
trailOffsetTicks = math.max(1, math.round(atr * trailAtrMult / syminfo.mintick))

// Exits are also submitted on the SIGNAL bar (with provisional levels) so the fill bar itself is
// protected; once the fill is confirmed, the same order IDs are re-issued with exact levels.
if strategy.position_size > 0 or longSignal
    // Break-even: once the position size drops below the initial fill (TP1 partial filled).
    if useBreakeven and useScaleOut and not beDone and not na(initialQty) and strategy.position_size > 0 and math.abs(strategy.position_size) < initialQty
        slAct  := strategy.position_avg_price + beOffsetTicks * syminfo.mintick
        beDone := true
    if useScaleOut
        strategy.exit("L-TP1", from_entry = "Long", qty_percent = scaleOutPct, stop = slAct, limit = tp1Act, comment_profit = "TP1", comment_loss = "SL")
        if runnerMode == "Fixed R Target"
            strategy.exit("L-TP2", from_entry = "Long", stop = slAct, limit = tp2Act, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "SL")
        else
            // Runner trails by ATR once price reaches the TP1 level.
            strategy.exit("L-TRL", from_entry = "Long", stop = slAct, trail_price = tp1Act, trail_offset = trailOffsetTicks, comment = "Trail")
    else
        strategy.exit("L-TP2", from_entry = "Long", stop = slAct, limit = tp2Act, comment_profit = "TP", comment_loss = "SL")

if strategy.position_size < 0 or shortSignal
    if useBreakeven and useScaleOut and not beDone and not na(initialQty) and strategy.position_size < 0 and math.abs(strategy.position_size) < initialQty
        slAct  := strategy.position_avg_price - beOffsetTicks * syminfo.mintick
        beDone := true
    if useScaleOut
        strategy.exit("S-TP1", from_entry = "Short", qty_percent = scaleOutPct, stop = slAct, limit = tp1Act, comment_profit = "TP1", comment_loss = "SL")
        if runnerMode == "Fixed R Target"
            strategy.exit("S-TP2", from_entry = "Short", stop = slAct, limit = tp2Act, comment_profit = "TP2", comment_loss = "SL")
        else
            strategy.exit("S-TRL", from_entry = "Short", stop = slAct, trail_price = tp1Act, trail_offset = trailOffsetTicks, comment = "Trail")
    else
        strategy.exit("S-TP2", from_entry = "Short", stop = slAct, limit = tp2Act, comment_profit = "TP", comment_loss = "SL")

// ── 7d. End-of-day flat & state reset ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
if eodNow
    strategy.cancel_all()
    if strategy.position_size != 0
        strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")
    pendingBar := na

justClosed = flat and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
if justClosed
    slAct      := na
    tp1Act     := na
    tp2Act     := na
    initialQty := na
    beDone     := false

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  8. PLOTTING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  (FVG/IFVG boxes are drawn in section 5. Everything else lives here.)

// HTF bias: EMA line + background tint (neutral gray when the bias filter is Off).
plot(showHtfEma ? htfEma : na, "HTF EMA", color = biasOff ? color.new(color.gray, 40) : biasBull ? color.new(#26a69a, 20) : color.new(#ef5350, 20), linewidth = 2)
bgcolor(showBiasBg and not biasOff ? (biasBull ? color.new(#26a69a, 94) : biasBear ? color.new(#ef5350, 94) : na) : na, title = "HTF bias tint")

// Entry signal markers. NOTE: the marker shows the SIGNAL bar — the fill happens on the next bar
// open (market) or when the limit is touched.
plotshape(longSignal,  "Long signal",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#26a69a, 0), size = size.small, text = "L")
plotshape(shortSignal, "Short signal", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(#ef5350, 0), size = size.small, text = "S")

// Active stop / targets while a position is open.
inLong  = strategy.position_size > 0
inShort = strategy.position_size < 0
plot(inLong or inShort ? slAct : na,                 "Stop loss",  color.new(#ef5350, 0),  2, plot.style_linebr)
plot((inLong or inShort) and useScaleOut ? tp1Act : na, "TP1",     color.new(#26a69a, 30), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(inLong or inShort ? tp2Act : na,                "Final TP",   color.new(#26a69a, 0),  2, plot.style_linebr)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  9. ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  Create an alert on this strategy → condition "FVG/IFVG Long Entry" (or Short) to drive
//  webhooks for automation. Placeholders resolve at alert time.

alertcondition(longSignal,  title = "FVG/IFVG Long Entry",  message = "FVG/IFVG LONG {{ticker}} {{interval}} @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(shortSignal, title = "FVG/IFVG Short Entry", message = "FVG/IFVG SHORT {{ticker}} {{interval}} @ {{close}}")
